  "query_preview": "..\n\nSynoptic Setup:  \n\nA weak cold front passing through the area will cause isolated\nshowers into Saturday morning along with a wind shift to the\nnorthwest. Otherwise, an upper-level high pressure system is \ndeveloping over the Four Corners region, allowing for anomalously \nstrong ridging to build over the west and move eastward into the \nregion by Monday morning. Seasonably average temperatures and dry \nconditions are expected this weekend before climbing to well above\naverage on Monday. Highs in the afternoon are expected to be in \nthe upper 70s to low 80s, with some places possibly climbing \nslightly higher.\n\nBeyond Monday, a weak cold front will move through Northeast \nMontana Tuesday morning. This should bring temperatures down \nslightly for the remainder of the week but will overall stay \nwarmer and drier than normal for this time of year. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n - No significant changes. Relatively high confidence for\n   seasonably warm temperatures and dry conditions next week with\n   well above average temperatures on Monday.\n\nKENZ",
